# .codx runtime state — written by the agents on every shift, never authored.
# ISO-8601 timestamps and task UUIDs in these files are high-entropy noise for
# the security scanner (1058 false `secret.high-entropy-token` findings) and they
# keep the working tree permanently dirty.
#
# Already-committed files are NOT covered by an ignore rule: drop them from the
# index once, without touching the files on disk. Paths are repo-root relative,
# so run this from the platform repo root (`codx-junior-platform/`); from inside
# `docs/` drop the leading `docs/` prefix. `--ignore-unmatch` makes both lines
# idempotent: a re-run is a no-op instead of a fatal "pathspec did not match",
# and `chat_turns/` currently matches no tracked file at all.
#   git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch docs/.codx/autonomy docs/.codx/harness docs/.codx/chat_turns
#   git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch docs/.codx/tasks/index.json docs/.codx/tasks/boards
autonomy/
harness/
chat_turns/
browser_sessions/
logs/

# Derived indexes: regenerated by the app from the card files on disk. They change
# on every card creation or move (+8 index.json / +9 board.json measured
# 2026-11-18T13:35Z), so they dirty the tree without carrying authored content.
# The cards themselves (`<board>/<column>/<name>.<uuid>.json`) are deliberately
# NOT ignored: they are the delivery record.
tasks/index.json
tasks/boards/
